The package audio-cpp provides CMake targets:

    find_package(audiocpp CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE audiocpp::audiocpp)

The C API is declared in <audiocpp.h>. See https://github.com/0xShug0/audio.cpp/blob/main/docs/c_api.md

With the "espeak" feature, eSpeak data is installed at share/audiocpp/espeak-ng-data.bin.
Static eSpeak looks for it next to the running executable, so copy it beside your
binary or pass it as the `espeak_data_path` session option.
